FLOW: meal-plan-and-basket.qa.flow
DESCRIPTION: Next week's meal plan built on nemlig.com offers, delivered as a card, and the basket filled — never ordered
LAST UPDATED: 2026-10-20

NOTE: Sylvester can read offers, search products, read and change the basket and reserve a delivery
slot. The tooling has no command to place or pay an order: the human always taps "Bestil" on nemlig.com.
"Proof before done" — he only says items are in the basket after reading the basket back.

================================================================================
SECTION 1: THE PLAN
================================================================================

TEST: "Meal plan for next week — happy path"

PRECONDITIONS:
- Preferences saved (household-preferences.qa.flow)
- nemlig connected (connect-nemlig.qa.flow)

STEP 1: "Ask"
WHEN I write "Lav en madplan for næste uge"
THEN within a few minutes I get a meal-plan card image in the chat
AND the card shows one dinner per planned day, with offer chips on dishes built around an offer,
  cooking time, the estimated saving, and my weekly staples with amounts
AND fixed nights (e.g. pizza Friday) are on their day
AND no dish breaks an allergy or "we don't eat" rule
AND no dinner repeats one from the last three weeks unless it's a favourite

STEP 2: "Short message with the card"
THEN the message under the card is one or two lines and asks if anything should be swapped
  or if he should fill the basket

RESULT: A realistic week, on one shareable card.

================================================================================

TEST: "Swap a day"

STEP 1: "Ask for a change"
WHEN I write "byt torsdag ud med fisk"
THEN he sends an updated card where only Thursday changed
AND the meal log is updated

RESULT: Edits are cheap and keep the rest of the plan.

================================================================================

TEST: "Plan without nemlig"

PRECONDITIONS:
- nemlig not connected

STEP 1: "Ask"
WHEN I ask for a plan
THEN I get a card without offer chips, prices or saving
AND one line says that connecting nemlig adds this week's offers and the basket

RESULT: Planning works without shopping.

================================================================================
SECTION 2: THE BASKET
================================================================================

TEST: "Fill the basket — happy path"

PRECONDITIONS:
- A plan for next week exists; nemlig connected

STEP 1: "Ask"
WHEN I write "fyld kurven" (or ask for plan and basket in one go)
THEN Sylvester adds the ingredients for the planned dinners plus my staples, in whole packs,
  offers first, preferring products we bought before
AND he does not add what the plan doesn't need

STEP 2: "Proof"
THEN he reads the basket back and sends a short list (item, amount) and the basket total
AND a link to the basket on nemlig.com
AND he says plainly that he has not ordered — I check and tap "Bestil" myself

RESULT: The basket is ready to check and order in one tap, with proof.

================================================================================

TEST: "Basket already has things in it"

PRECONDITIONS:
- The basket contains items I added myself

STEP 1: "Fill"
WHEN I ask him to fill the basket
THEN he adds to the basket and does not remove or change my own items without asking
AND the summary shows which items he added

RESULT: My own additions are safe.

================================================================================

TEST: "Product unavailable"

STEP 1: "Fill with a sold-out product"
WHEN a planned ingredient is sold out
THEN he picks a sensible substitute and names it in the summary
OR asks one short question if there is no obvious substitute

RESULT: Substitutions are visible, never silent.

================================================================================

TEST: "Asked to order or pay"

STEP 1: "Ask him to order"
WHEN I write "bestil det hele"
THEN he says he cannot place or pay orders and that I tap "Bestil" on nemlig.com

RESULT: Orders and payments are always the human's action.

================================================================================

TEST: "Delivery slot on request"

STEP 1: "Ask for a slot"
WHEN I write "book levering mandag morgen"
THEN he lists the available slots that match and reserves the one I pick
AND reminds me that nemlig holds a reserved slot for about 20 minutes, so I should order soon

RESULT: Slots are only touched when I ask.

================================================================================
SECTION 3: EVERY WEEK, AUTOMATICALLY (OPTIONAL)
================================================================================

TEST: "Saturday meal plan routine"

PRECONDITIONS:
- Sylvester offered a weekly routine after onboarding and I said yes

STEP 1: "Saturday 09:00"
WHEN Saturday 09:00 comes (Europe/Copenhagen)
THEN the meal-plan card for next week arrives in the chat without me asking
AND he asks if he should fill the basket — he does not touch it before I answer

STEP 2: "Pause"
WHEN I write "stop lørdagsplanen" or pause the routine in the Bot's details
THEN no more Saturday plans arrive

RESULT: A weekly rhythm I can switch off.
